      "title": "DepthPro2 \u2014 Image to Depth",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## DepthPro2 \u2014 Image to Depth\n\nMetric depth (meters) from a single photo with [Apple Depth Pro 2](https://huggingface.co/apple/DepthPro2).\n\n**Loader**\n- Copy the shipped `example.png` into `ComfyUI/input/` before running this example. The main checkpoint loads without the focal checkpoint; automatic estimation downloads and initializes the focal model on its first use, while an explicit focal pixel input skips it.\n- `model`: `depthpro2-s/b/l/h` download automatically into `models/depthpro2` on first use (S: 97 MB, H+: 3.5 GB). Larger = sharper and steadier.\n- `precision`: `auto` uses ComfyUI's session dtype on the accelerator (usually fp16) and fp32 on CPU. `fp8` compresses weight storage and dequantizes on every forward; it is not an fp8 matrix-multiply kernel. The focal estimator's trunk follows the compute dtype while its heads stay fp32. No calibrated cross-precision accuracy claim is made.\n\n**Estimate**\n- `focal_length_mm`: lens focal length as a 35mm-equivalent in mm (24, 35, 50\u2026 \u2014 the EXIF FocalLengthIn35mmFilm value); `0` estimates it automatically while the **Estimate focal length** toggle is on (default) \u2014 with it off, an explicit positive focal length is required. A linked `focal_length_px` overrides the mm value, including a linked `0.0` that requests estimation. Depth in meters scales linearly with focal length \u2014 set it if you know it. For cine cameras (physical mm + sensor size), use the **DepthPro2 Focal Length** node and link its output instead.\n- `max_size`: `0` chooses a budget-aware processing resolution, `-1` uses native resolution, and a positive value caps the longest side. Outputs are restored to the input size.\n\n**Outputs**\n- `depth_image`: normalized inverse depth, near white / far black (preview / ControlNet).\n- `depth_meters`: raw metric depth `(T, H, W)`, `inf` at sky.\n- `sky_mask`: MASK, 1 at sky \u2014 a ready-made comp holdout.\n- `focal_length_px`: focal used, in pixels of the input.\n\n**Colorize**\n- `colormap`: `turbo` is Apple's preview colormap (dark blue far, red/white near); scale anchored on the nearest point + 20% headroom. Also `viridis`, `inferno`, `magma`, `plasma`, `gray`.\n\nWeights are licensed for **non-commercial research only** (Apple AMLR)."
      ]
    },
